  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Halle de Grimaud is an organic, local grocery (fruit and vegetables, butcher-deli, dairy and cheese, farm eggs, wine cellar) that also caters. On weekends, it turns into an oyster bar with a guinguette vibe, with a tasting terrace available for customers to linger.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The "Pets accepted" mention appears among the services in the Grimaud tourist office listing (relayed by Visit Var, updated on 09/02/2026, and by Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme). The listing concerns the establishment as a whole: it does not say whether pets are admitted in the grocery, on the tasting terrace or at the oyster bar. It also mentions parking and a site accessible to people with reduced mobility.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the weekend oyster bar is especially lively. Check the busy hours if you prefer a calmer atmosphere with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Opening hours</h2>
      <p>Visit Var announces opening every day from 8am to 7:30pm, from 1 January to 31 December, specifying that days and hours should be checked with the establishment. A market directory instead indicates opening Tuesday to Sunday: the two versions differ. Phone: 04 94 56 06 80; website: lahalledegrimaud.com.</p>

      <h2>Check before you go</h2>
      <p>Call before coming to confirm opening days, the oyster bar days and whether your dog may come in or only wait for you on the terrace.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The medieval village of Grimaud and its lanes, as well as the lakeside town of Port Grimaud, are a few minutes away by car to extend the outing.</p>
